I would suggest a new menu item, except with better word choice than
the examples below. "Apply to a steed" is kind of weird-sounding.

    'a'
    Apply what?  (the saddlebags)
    Your saddlebags are empty. Do what?
    i - Put something into the saddlebags
    s - Apply the saddlebags to a steed

    'a'
    Apply what?  (the saddlebags)
    Do what?
    o - Take something out of the saddlebags
    i - Put something into the saddlebags
    b - Both of the above
    s - Apply the saddlebags to a steed

Here are some more considerations.

      Are saddlebags a separate item from the existing "saddle"?
      If yes:
        Can saddlebags be applied to an unsaddled steed?
        Can saddlebags be affixed to a saddle in your inventory?
        Can a saddle be removed without removing the saddlebags first?
      If no:
        Remember that knights start with a saddle.
      Can saddlebags hold a finite number of items?
      If no:
        Are they magical?
          Does blessing them help?
          Does cursing them hurt?
        If yes:
          Can they explode?[1]
      Do heavy saddlebags slow down a steed?
      Can too-heavy saddlebags kill a steed?
      Do they burn?
      Do they rot?

Also, an amusing question: Is it possible for a polymorphed player to
wear a saddle? If so, how? And would he be able to loot his own saddlebags?

my $.02,
-Arthur

[1] - Non-magical items shouldn't explode. Unless they're land mines.


